Define "close to fit well". The topic has a long (and somehow sad) history on SEMnet. Maybe you can ask this question there?

Ultimately, the question is whether the chi-square test is "useful" and whether the alternative fit indices are "useful". Ultimately, this involves a seemingly simple question: How do *you* define the term "model"?

There is a very good video on the subject by Mikko on YouTube: https://youtu.be/L-mjMlyl2Xg

HTH

Christian

