You may have somehow loaded the namespace of semTools (e.g., do something like semTools::xxx) directly or indirectly before using library(semTools) to load the library. I can reproduce your error as below. See the first line, semTools::mardiaKurtosis(), which is called before calling library(semTools):
semTools::mardiaKurtosis(matrix(rnorm(10), ncol = 1))
#>        b2d          z          p
#>  1.0630483 -1.2502969  0.2111911

library(semTools)
