Sorry to hear about that. You may need help from Terrence. I vaguely recall a similar problem was discussed before but forgot where.

Given that you could run summary() in Windows but not in Mac, you can type showMethods("summary") and compare the results:

When summary() could run successfully on a lavaan.mi object, this is what displayed on my computer:

> showMethods("summary")
Function: summary (package base)
object="ANY"
object="BootMiss"
object="diagonalMatrix"
object="EFA"
object="FitDiff"
object="lavaan"
object="lavaan.mi"
object="lavaanList"
object="measEq.syntax"
object="mle"
object="Net"
object="permuteMeasEq"
object="sparseMatrix"
object="twostage"

When I intentionally made the call failed (by calling semTools::xxx first), this is what displayed:

> showMethods("summary")
Function: summary (package base)
object="ANY"
object="diagonalMatrix"
object="lavaan"
object="lavaan.mi"
    (inherited from: object="lavaanList")
object="lavaanList"
object="mle"
object="sparseMatrix"

The summary-method for many classes in semTools are not registered in the second case, in which the error occurred. Even though the summary-method for lavaan.mi is registered, maybe it is actually the lavaan's method for lavaanList that is used, not the one in semTools. (But I am not not sure.)

I do not know the possible source of the difference other than calling semTools::xxx first. Perhaps there are other causes that can lead to the same problem.

Anyway, maybe the info above can help others to figure out what happened.

-- Shu Fai

