> The summary-method for many classes in semTools are not registered in the second case, in which the error occurred. Even though the summary-method for lavaan.mi is registered, maybe it is actually the lavaan's method for lavaanList that is used, not the one in semTools. (But I am not not sure.)
>
> I do not know the possible source of the difference other than calling semTools::xxx first. Perhaps there are other causes that can lead to the same problem.
>
> Anyway, maybe the info above can help others to figure out what happened.
>
> -- Shu Fai
