Here the model
CFA_model2 <- '
 IC =~ Q19_1 + Q19_2 + Q19_3
 PC =~ Q19_4 + Q19_5 + Q19_6
 ATT =~ ATT_1 + ATT_2
 SN =~ SN_1 + SN_2
 PBC =~ PBC1_1 + PBC2_1
 INT =~ INT_1 + INT_2 + INT_3'

I run the following functions:
#configural invariance
fit1 <- cfa(CFA_model2, data = df_cleaned1,  meanstructure=T, estimator="WLSMV", group = "residence")

# weak invariance
fit2 <- cfa(CFA_model2, data = df_cleaned1,  meanstructure=T, estimator="WLSMV", group = "residence", std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE,   group.equal = "loadings")

Then:
lavTestLRT(fit1, fit2)
Results:
Df AIC BIC Chisq Chisq diff Df diff Pr(>Chisq) fit1 150 210.74
fit2 159 290.84 84.096 9 2.472e-14 ***

So what I did was running other tests:
lavInspect(fit2, "sampstat")
lavTech(fit2, "sampstat")
lavTestScore(fit2)
parTable(fit2)

lavTestScore suggested the following significant psths:
.p9. == .p81. 29.725  1   0.000
 .p10. == .p82. 29.725  1   0.000
  .p11. == .p83. 35.825  1   0.000
 .p12. == .p84. 35.825  1   0.000
which correspond to the following ones (using parTable)
SN =~  SN_1       SN =~   SN_2 PBC =~ PBC1_1  PBC =~ PBC2_1  IC =~ Q19_3 PC =~  Q19_4  PC =~ Q19_6  So what I did was the following:
fit2_1 <- cfa(CFA_model2, data = df_cleaned1,  meanstructure=T, estimator="WLSMV", group = "residence", std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE, group.partial = c("SN_1~ 1","SN_2~1", " PBC1_1~1",  "PBC2_1~1",   "Q19_3~1", " Q19_4~1", "  Q19_6~1"),  group.equal = "loadings")
lavTestLRT(fit1, fit2_1)
Results:
Df AIC BIC Chisq Chisq diff Df diff Pr(>Chisq) fit1 150 210.74 fit2_1 159 290.84 84.096 9 2.472e-14 ***

But the result of the chi-square is always the same, so I guess I am doing something wrong here. I am not sure how to constrain those parameters. I already read the following conversations https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/AaILttPQFGs, https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/fzIg5jrxIAI/m/xoq5l803AAAJ, but still not able to figure out what I am doing wrong. Some help would be really appreciated!

