OK, I nailed it and I am sharing the code that did it:

SEM_model4<-'
          #regressions model
          ZEA4items~b1*ZEC3dim+b2*ZESEsum+b3*ZESExZEC
          ZEA2~c*ZEA4items+a1*ZEC3dim+a2*SPOL+a3*DRUZ_BINAR

          ZEC3dim~~ZESExZEC
          ZEC3dim~~ZESEsum
          ZESEsum~~ZESExZEC

          # key
          ## IV - ZEC3dim
          ## Z - ZESExZEC
          ## M - ZEA4items
          ## DV - ZEA2
          ## ESE - ZESEsum
          ## SPOL - SPOL
          ## DRUZ - DRUZ_BIN

          #indirect
          indirect_IV_M_DV:=b1*c
          indirect_Z_M_DV:=b3*c
          indirect_ESE_M_DV:=b2*c

          #direct
          direct_IV_M:=c
          direct_Z_M:=b3
          direct_IV_M:=b1
          direct_ESE_M:=b2
          direct_IV_DV:=a1
          direct_SPOL_DV:=a2
          direct_DRUZ_DV:=a3

          #total
          Total_IV_DV:=b1*c+a1
          Total_Z_DV:=b3*c+0
          '
The CI values are not the same as with my supervisor but they are sig in the same way. So I got ideas in this group and I thank you. :)

