lavaan's output should indicate the free parameters.  If you have 4 observed variables in your model, 8 free parameters and 1 degree of freedom, then it sounds like only 1 of your predictor variables is being treated as exogenous. Applying fixed.x=T to one of your two predictors would mean that you have 9 elements of the covariance matrix available, and could give you 8 free parameters. Obtaining that result, however, may involve an error in your syntax. The lavaan::summary() function or the lavaan::parameterEstimates() function will show you exactly which parameter estimates are free. In summary()< those are the parameter estimates that have estimated standard errors.

